cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
title: "Auditing the Wind Tunnel: the Twin-Enrichment Closed Form at Reachable omega, and the Marginal-versus-Per-Centre Distinction"
abstract: >-
  Part XXVIII of the Arithmetic Geodynamics on the 6N Skeleton series.
  An empirical audit, against a real prime sieve to 6N <= 2e8 (813,370 twin
  centres), of the Part XXIII wind-tunnel extrapolation of twin-centre
  enrichment to the omega=15 primorial (x7.03). Establishes that the per-prime
  modifier q/(q-2) is exact and multiplicative on the reachable range, derives
  the correct per-centre likelihood C * prod (q-1)/(q-3) with C = 0.7216, and
  distinguishes the x7.03 upper envelope from the typical omega-stratified
  enrichment.
